: at_ms=12832
data: {"asset_version_id": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-00000000a005", "conversation_id": "00000000000000000000a001", "message_id": "00000000000000000000a003", "event": "FINAL_RESPONSE", "content": {"asset_version_id": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-00000000a005", "conversation_id": "00000000000000000000a001", "message_id": "00000000000000000000a003", "query": "Explain how HTTPS works in about 400 words. Include a markdown table comparing TLS 1.2 and TLS 1.3, a short code block, and a mermaid sequence diagram in a fenced code block.", "response": "# How HTTPS Works\n\nHTTPS (Hypertext Transfer Protocol Secure) is the secure version of HTTP, encrypting data exchanged between a client (browser) and a server using **TLS (Transport Layer Security)**. This ensures confidentiality, integrity, and authentication of data in transit.\n\n## The Process Overview\n\n1. **TCP Connection**: The client establishes a TCP connection with the server (typically port 443).\n2. **TLS Handshake**: Client and server negotiate encryption parameters, exchange certificates, and establish a shared secret key.\n3. **Certificate Verification**: The client verifies the server's certificate against trusted Certificate Authorities (CAs) to confirm identity.\n4. **Symmetric Encryption**: Once the handshake completes, both parties use symmetric encryption (faster than asymmetric) to encrypt all subsequent data.\n5. **Secure Data Transfer**: HTTP requests and responses are now encrypted, protecting against eavesdropping and tampering.\n\n## Sequence Diagram\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    participant Client\n    participant Server\n\n    Client->>Server: ClientHello (supported ciphers, TLS version)\n    Server->>Client: ServerHello (chosen cipher, certificate)\n    Client->>Client: Verify certificate against CA\n    Client->>Server: Key Exchange (pre-master secret, encrypted)\n    Server->>Client: Finished (handshake complete)\n    Client->>Server: Finished (handshake complete)\n    Note over Client,Server: Symmetric session key established\n    Client->>Server: Encrypted HTTP Request\n    Server->>Client: Encrypted HTTP Response\n```\n\n## TLS 1.2 vs TLS 1.3\n\n| Feature | TLS 1.2 | TLS 1.3 |\n|---|---|---|\n| Handshake Round Trips | 2 round trips | 1 round trip (0-RTT possible) |\n| Handshake Speed | Slower | Faster |\n| Supported Cipher Suites | Many (including weaker ones like RC4, CBC) | Reduced, only strong AEAD ciphers |\n| Forward Secrecy | Optional | Mandatory |\n| Key Exchange | RSA, DH, ECDHE | Only ECDHE (RSA key exchange removed) |\n| Renegotiation | Allowed (security risk) | Removed |\n| Compression | Supported (vulnerable to CRIME attack) | Removed |\n| Static RSA Support | Yes | No |\n| Released | 2008 | 2018 |\n\n## Example: Checking HTTPS in Code\n\nHere's a simple Python example using the `requests` library to make a secure HTTPS request and inspect the TLS version:\n\n```python\nimport requests\nimport ssl\n\nresponse = requests.get(\"https://example.com\")\nprint(\"Status Code:\", response.status_code)\nprint(\"Negotiated Protocol:\", response.raw.connection.sock.version())\n```\n\n## Why HTTPS Matters\n\n- **Confidentiality**: Encrypts data so attackers can't read intercepted traffic.\n- **Integrity**: Detects any tampering with data in transit.\n- **Authentication**: Confirms you're communicating with the legitimate server, not an imposter.\n\nTLS 1.3's streamlined handshake and removal of vulnerable legacy features make it significantly faster and more secure than TLS 1.2, which is why most modern browsers and servers now prioritize it by default.", "additional_model_output": {"logprobs": {"raw_response": {"content": []}}}, "metrics": {"total_tokens": 3238, "total_cost": 0.01638, "prompt_tokens": 2000, "completion_tokens": 1238, "total_llm_time": 11.119148015975952, "successful_requests": 1, "total_time": 12.747}, "sources": [], "citation": [], "llm_citation": null, "traces": [], "debug_trace_ids": [], "add_ons": {}, "evals": {}, "artifacts": [], "message_status": "SUCCESS", "artifacts_generated": {"files": []}, "context_usage": {"context_window": 872000, "context_usage_pct": 0.23, "overhead_tokens": 38, "tokens_until_compaction": -1, "compaction_count": 0, "compaction_available": false, "overhead_bound": false}}, "status": "SUCCESS"}

